{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MatrixSchurCommutant"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.markovGram_transports_to_hodge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.markovGram_transports_to_hodge","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L175-L196","doc":"**Sub-piece (ii), correctly reduced.** Given the Hecke-side S₅ symmetry of the\nMarkov Gram (conjugator `T` to the geometric S₅ action `ρS`), the irreducibility\nof `ρS` (⇒ scalar commutant, #4182), and a unit Hodge form, the transported Markov\nGram `Tᵀ · G_Markov · T` is a scalar multiple of the Hodge form. This is the\ngenuine reduction the generator-intertwiner failed to be: its premise is\nSATISFIABLE (`ρS'`, `ρS` share the `(4,1)` character, no trace obstruction).\nSTRICT: no `HeckeSideS5Symmetry` instance for the actual τ is registered; the\nexistence of the Tits-transported symmetry with `T = τ` is the honest open input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.markov_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.markov_inv","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L173-L173","doc":"The Markov Gram is invariant under the Hecke-side S₅ action `ρS'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.intertwines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.intertwines","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L171-L171","doc":"`T` conjugates `ρS'` to `ρS` (same `(4,1)` character ⇒ trace-consistent). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.T","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L169-L169","doc":"Conjugator to the geometric S₅ action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.ρS'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.ρS'","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L167-L167","doc":"The S₅ action on the Hecke module space (the Tits-transported action). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry.mk","kind":"ctor","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.HeckeSideS5Symmetry","kind":"structure","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L151-L173","doc":"**The Hecke-side S₅ symmetry — the correct, SATISFIABLE form of sub-piece (ii).**\nWhere `GeneratorIntertwiner` is obstructed (`intertwiner_trace_eq`), this posits\nthe honest object: an S₅ action `ρS'` **on the Hecke module space** under which the\nMarkov Gram is invariant, together with a conjugator `T` to the geometric S₅\naction `ρS` (`ρS' s * T = T * ρS s`).\n\n**This premise is satisfiable** (unlike the generator one): `ρS'` and `ρS` are both\nthe `(4,1)` S₅-irrep, so they share a character — the `intertwiner_trace_eq`\nobstruction does NOT apply (`trace ρS' s = trace ρS s` holds), and a conjugating\n`T` exists by Schur. And the Markov Gram admits such a `ρS'` because the Tits\n`*`-iso realises the S₅ symmetry on `H₅(q₀)`'s `(4,1)` block (the Markov/`*`-form\nis S₅-invariant for the Tits-transported action, NOT for the Hecke generators).\nThe OPEN categorical claim (no instance registered) is that the archimedean functor\nτ realises `T` for the ACTUAL Markov form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.tauImage_proportional_hodge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.tauImage_proportional_hodge","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L120-L149","doc":"**General pullback assembly** (NOT a reduction of sub-piece ii — see the\ncaveat). Given *any* `GeneratorIntertwiner` on `std`, S₅-irreducibility of `ρS`\n(discharging scalar-commutant via `MatrixSchurCommutant`), a unit Hodge form\n`G_H`, and invariance of the Hodge form (`ρS`) and the Markov Gram `G_M` (`ρH`),\nthe pulled-back Markov Gram `Pᵀ * G_M * P` is a scalar multiple of `G_H`.\n\n⚠ **This does NOT reduce (ii)** for the actual Hecke/S₅ actions: by\n`intertwiner_trace_eq` the hypothesis `GeneratorIntertwiner ρH ρS` is\n**unsatisfiable** there (`trace σ₁ ≈ 2.43 ≠ 2`). The theorem is a true statement\nabout an *abstract* form-preserving intertwiner; the real τ-correspondence is the\nTits `*`-iso conjugator, which is **not** a `GeneratorIntertwiner` and is not\nsupplied here. STRICT: no instance for the actual τ is exhibited; `1/(8π)` stays\nphase-4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.intertwiner_trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.intertwiner_trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L99-L118","doc":"**Obstruction — a generator-intertwiner forces equal generator traces.** If\n`P` is a unit intertwining `ρH` and `ρS`, then `(ρH s).trace = (ρS s).trace` for\nevery `s`, since `ρH s = P (ρS s) P⁻¹` is a conjugate.\n\nThis **rules out** a generator-intertwiner between the Hecke and S₅ actions on\n`std`: the Hecke generator `σ₁` has `trace = 3q₀ − q₀⁻¹ ≈ 2.43` (eigenvalues\n`q₀,q₀,q₀,−q₀⁻¹`), while an S₅ transposition on `std` has `trace = 2`\n(fixed-points − 1). `2.43 ≠ 2`, so no `GeneratorIntertwiner` exists at `q₀ ≠ 1`.\nHence sub-piece (ii) is **not** a generator-intertwiner; the correct object is the\nTits `*`-iso conjugator (open). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.intertwines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.intertwines","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Intertwining relation between the two generator actions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L95-L95","doc":"`P` is invertible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.P","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.P","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The intertwiner matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner.mk","kind":"ctor","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.GeneratorIntertwiner","kind":"structure","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L80-L97","doc":"**A generator-level intertwiner** `P` between two actions `ρH`, `ρS`:\n`ρH s * P = P * ρS s`, `P` invertible.\n\n⚠ **This is NOT satisfiable for the (Hecke-generator, S₅-generator) actions on\n`std` at `q₀ ≠ 1`** — see `intertwiner_trace_eq` below. The Hecke generator\n`σᵢ` (eigenvalues `q₀,−q₀⁻¹`) is not conjugate to an S₅ transposition\n(eigenvalues `1,−1`), so no such `P` exists. The *actual* τ-correspondence is the\n**Tits `*`-algebra iso** `H₅(q₀) ≅ ℂ[S₅]` on the `(4,1)` block (a Skolem–Noether\nconjugator sending `σᵢ` to a *non-generator* element), which this generator\nstructure does **not** model. Kept only to state the general pullback assembly\nand to carry the obstruction lemma. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.invariantForm_pullback","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauS5EquivarianceReduction.invariantForm_pullback","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauS5EquivarianceReduction.lean#L61-L78","doc":"**Transport of an invariant form along an intertwiner.** If `P` intertwines\n`ρH` and `ρS` (`ρH s * P = P * ρS s`) and `M` is a `ρH`-invariant form, then\n`Pᵀ * M * P` is a `ρS`-invariant form. This is the linear-algebra content of\n\"an S₅-equivariant τ carries the Markov Gram to an S₅-invariant form.\" ","signatureChunk":0}]}